<title>BRAZIL: Lloyds nears closing on Brazil bank deal.</title>
<headline>Lloyds nears closing on Brazil bank deal.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Banco Multiplic expects to conclude the sale of assets to its partner Lloyds Bank Plc in 180 days, a major shareholder of the Brazilian bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a process of 180 days,&quot; said Ronaldo Cesar Coelho, who owns 50 percent of holding company Multiplic Empreendimentos, which has a 50 percent stake in Banco Multiplic.</p>
<p>Earlier Tuesday, Lloyds Bank in Brazil said in a statement it planned to dissolve a 19-year-old partnership with Multiplic, though no agreement had been formalized yet.</p>
</text>
